  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'An object is placed 10 cm in front of a concave mirror of radius of curvature 15 cm. Calculate the position, nature and magnification of the image. (3 marks)', 'f = R/2 = 15/2 = 7.5 cm (concave mirror).
Using 1/f = 1/u + 1/v with distances in front of the mirror positive: 1/v = 1/7.5 − 1/10 = (4 − 3)/30 = 1/30, so v = 30 cm.
(New Cartesian signs: u = −10, f = −7.5 give v = −30 cm - the same position.)
The image is 30 cm in front of the mirror (on the same side as the object): it is real and inverted.
Magnification m = −v/u = −30/10 = −3: the image is three times the size of the object and inverted. (The object lies between F and C, so the image lies beyond C.)', null, '[{"point": "f = R/2 = 7.5 cm; mirror formula 1/f = 1/u + 1/v (real-is-positive) gives 1/v = 1/7.5 − 1/10 = 1/30", "marks": 1}, {"point": "v = 30 cm in front of the mirror", "marks": 1}, {"point": "Real and inverted; m = −v/u = −3 (three times enlarged)", "marks": 1}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
